==Enemy==
Those Guys have fairly high health and low damage but attack rather quickly, somewhat like [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cat]]. Their damage is surprisingly higher than [[Snache]] and [[Doge]], but they aren't threatening at all outside of the early-game.

==Strategy==
Those Guys can be somewhat hard for newer players because they have above-average health and only one knockback. However, one set of Those Guys is easily killable with an [[Axe Cat (Normal Cat)|Axe Cat]] or even multiple [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Basic Cats]]. Without sufficient [[Treasure]]s or Cat Cannon Power upgrades, Those Guys can even survive one hit from the [[Cat Cannon]].

When there are multiple clumps of them, Those Guys can quickly turn into a nuisance, like in [[Denmark (Empire of Cats)|Denmark/Shizuoka]]. In these cases, [[Bird Cat (Normal Cat)|Bird Cat]], [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Titan Cat]] or any other unit with [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attack]] can take care of them. Later on, though, they will turn into meatshields for harder enemies, like [[Le'boin]], [[Master A.]] or [[Camelle]]. To clear out a group of them, [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Gross Cat]] or other [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave Attackers]] can be used.

Later on, Those Guys become irrelevant since their stats are too low to be a serious threat. They're mostly spawned to give the player quick money, or to stop your attackers from hitting the main threat. The main exception is their appearance in [[The Noble Tribe]].

