==Variants==
{{Variant
|original = Those Guys
|Fireworks Guys (High-Yield)
|A harmless pair of stick figures with a firework cannon. Can be found in many events.
|Fireworks Guys (Low-Yield)
|A variant of Fireworks Guys whose fireworks go a little lower for visual diversity. They also have double the range for some reason.
|Trolly Blogger
|An enemy commonly seen in later [[Legend Stages]]. Moves faster, with high range for a peon, rapid area attacks and 15% chance to cause knockback.
|Mr. Angel
|An [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] variant of Trolly Blogger. Moves even faster, gets knocked back more times and has a chance to weaken cats.
|Glowstick Guys
|A much weaker variant of Those Guys wearing neon colored bandanas and holding penlights with the same color. Found in the [[Crazed Moneko]] and [[Hatsune Miku Collaboration Event#Hatsune Miku|Hatsune Miku]] Stages.
|The Thrillerz
|A [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] variant of Those Guys, introduced in [[Into the Future]] Chapter 2's [[Zombie Outbreaks]]. They have higher health, damage and speed, revive once with 100% health and can burrow twice.
|Cerberus Kids
|An [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] variant of Those Guys. They have a chance to [[Freeze|freeze]] units they hit for 4 seconds, but are still [[Single Attack]] and have short range.
|Miz Devil
|An Aku variant of Mr. Angel. Has shorter range to allow for easier pushing, has one knockback as opposed to eight, and most of her health comes in the form of a [[Shield]].
|Archangel Exiel
|A [[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus]] variant of Mr. Angel that appears in the [[Divine Archangel Strikes]] gauntlet. He has amazing stats across the board as well as [[Omni Strike]], [[Warp]], and [[Weaken]] abilities.
|Omens
|A Colossus variant of Cerberus Kids introduced as the boss of [[Attack of the Omens]], with vastly improved stats, occasional [[Surge Attack|Surges]], and the ability to hit three times per attack.
|Fireworks Gang
|A bigger trio of stick figures, though not as large as Omens. They have very high health and DPS for a Those Guys variant, attack as fast as a [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]] and have surprisingly long reach, with 250 range, 400 Omni Strike and a 20% chance to create a level 1 Surge at 150~650.
}}

