==Trivia==
*Those Guys are a possible reference to [[wikia:gradius:Koitsu, Aitsu, Soitsu and Doitsu|Koitsu, Aitsu, Soitsu and Doitsu]] from the ''[[wikipedia:Parodius|Parodius]]'' series. In addition to being featureless stick figures, Those Guys have a similar Japanese name (Rei no Yatsu) and their Japanese description states that they are too insecure to fight outside of a group, much like how the ''Parodius'' stickmen are only useful in pairs in ''[[wikia:gradius:Yu-Gi-Oh! (series)|Yu-Gi-Oh!]]''.
**Although Those Guys only appear in groups of three, one short of the four stickmen in ''Parodius'', there is a fourth member of Those Guys who fights alone: [[Trolly Blogger]].
*They are currently the only enemy to have multiple [[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus]] variants, those being [[Archangel Exiel]] and [[Omens]].
*They appear in the most levels throughout the game excluding [[Ms. Sign]], even more than [[Doge]].
*Those Guys placed #1 in [[Year's End Event#Most Defeated 2019|Most Defeated 2019]], [[Year's End Event#Most Appearances 2020|Most Appearances 2020]] and [[Lunar New Year#Top 5 Most Seen Enemies, 2021!|Top 5 Most Seen Enemies, 2021!]].
*Prior to [[Version 15.1 Update|Version 15.1]], "all of them are quite rich." had its own line after "Surprisingly," in Those Guys' description.

